From: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: sc27xx-fgu: name the supply "battery"

ROCKNIX finds the battery by name: battery_percent() in 001-functions reads
POWER_SUPPLY_CAPACITY from /sys/class/power_supply/[Bb][Aa][Tt]*/uevent. The
SC27xx fuel gauge registers as "sc27xx-fgu", so nothing matches, the battery
level is empty, powerstate fails its arithmetic every two seconds and the
low-battery warning never fires. Register under "battery", as most fuel
gauges do. Nothing looks the supply up by its old name: the chargers and the
board's DT reach it through monitored-battery and phandles.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/sc27xx_fuel_gauge.c
@@ -891,7 +891,7 @@
 };
 
 static const struct power_supply_desc sc27xx_fgu_desc = {
-	.name			= "sc27xx-fgu",
+	.name			= "battery",
 	.type			= POWER_SUPPLY_TYPE_BATTERY,
 	.properties		= sc27xx_fgu_props,
 	.num_properties		= ARRAY_SIZE(sc27xx_fgu_props),
